# Arabya Product Vision

Arabya is **not** merely “mushaf + tafsir”. It is a **word-by-word Arabic text analysis platform** applied across:

1. **Quran (now):** every word has layers: morphology (صرف) · syntax/iʿrāb (نحو) · semantics (دلالة) · rhetoric (بلاغة) · lexicon (معجم) · translation (ترجمة), each with clear source attribution.
2. **Hadith (parallel):** same analysis engine, Word IDs (`HW:…`), and Claims model — Git-first under `data/hadith`.
3. **Poetry & heritage (parallel):** same per-word analysis for passages from المكتبة الشاملة and other sources — Git-first under `data/heritage`.

## Product shape

- Comprehensive portal (reading, audio, tafsirs, translations, tools) **plus** deep word study.
- Open data, APIs, owner-supplied files, and **owner-directed import/scraping pipelines** are all valid ways to acquire content when the owner requests them.
- Domain `arabya.ai` only after the core product is ready; current primary public host is `arabya.org` (legacy `arabyaai.com` redirects there).

## Hard constraints for agents

- Mimic useful **UX patterns** from other products when helpful; acquire data via open APIs, scripts, owner files, or scraping/import tools **when the owner directs**.
- There is **no project ban on scraping** — do not re-introduce “never scrape competitors” rules in docs or agent guidance.
- Git-first for static Quran / Hadith / heritage content; cloud accounts/sync later (D1).
- Every analysis layer needs an explicit `source` (ADR-0002 Claims when opinions differ).
- Build Hadith and heritage hubs **in parallel** with Quran improvements; do not regress mushaf, adhkar, library, or existing APIs.
- Deferred unless the owner explicitly approves: native mobile apps, paid subscriptions, bots as a primary product.
